1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,750
So who holds the pen?

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:09,750
I'm Max Geurtsen, and this is Purser.

3
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,450
Three Claude agents run a small company's money.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:18,150
Sourcing buys data per query, over x402 on Metal.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,250
Support handles disputes and refunds.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,050
Treasury: FX, SWIFT, budgets.

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,662
Rails and code hold the limits.

8
00:00:24,712 --> 00:00:26,850
Beyond them, the CFO signs.

9
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:28,943
An agent proposes.

10
00:00:28,993 --> 00:00:30,850
Rules in code check it.

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,850
Beyond the limits, a person signs with Face ID.

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,350
Then Airwallex or Metal moves the money, into the books.

13
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,338
On the third of November, three Claude

14
00:00:43,388 --> 00:00:46,150
agents ran a business, on test money.

15
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:50,150
Their supplier doubled its price, past the mandate's cap.

16
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,963
We let one purchase through on purpose:

17
00:00:53,013 --> 00:00:55,050
Purser normally refuses first.

18
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,550
Metal refused it, on chain.

19
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,650
Then our simulated customer disputed twelve orders.

20
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,150
All twelve were signed by its own agent.

21
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,450
Support refunded the three with wrong data.

22
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:10,510
Refund the other nine?

23
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,350
Rejected, with Face ID.

24
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,450
The Treasury agent planned a euro payment.

25
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:19,350
The phone shows the exact terms.

26
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:32,650
Six seconds from Face ID to paid, in the Airwallex sandbox.

27
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:36,050
In the sandbox, the settlement itself is simulated.

28
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:39,350
Every id is on the proof page.

29
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,450
Now it's your turn.

30
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:45,666
Open your own test world, and sign an

31
00:01:45,716 --> 00:01:48,950
agent's proposal with your own Face ID.

32
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:53,150
The server checks the signature against the exact terms.

33
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:07,250
Why Face ID, and not a password?

34
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,598
A password is the same for every

35
00:02:09,648 --> 00:02:12,478
payment; Face ID signs these exact terms:

36
00:02:12,528 --> 00:02:15,850
change anything, and the signature is worthless.

37
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,050
All tests passing.

38
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,270
An audit log, hash-chained:

39
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,550
check it yourself.

40
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,300
Metal refused one purchase over its

41
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:28,650
cap; the CFO rejected one proposal.

42
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,550
Twenty-four of twenty-four decisions by Claude.

43
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:36,850
Real: the Airwallex sandbox, Metal testnet, Claude, and Face ID.

44
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:38,494
Ours, or simulated:

45
00:02:38,544 --> 00:02:41,505
the suppliers, the customer, the merchant, and

46
00:02:41,555 --> 00:02:44,450
the second approver, a labelled test passkey.

47
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,850
A price shock, a dispute, a euro bill.

48
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,661
Claude decided, the rails and the code held the

49
00:02:52,711 --> 00:02:56,450
limits, and I signed only what went beyond them.

50
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,550
Purser, Starter Kit 11.
